SELinux: let genfscon label filesystems whose behaviour is GENFS

vfat has no xattrs, so files on the user store are labelled from genfscon --
but genfscon is only consulted for a superblock marked SE_SBGENFS, and the
3.0.35 tree marks proc, debugfs, sysfs and pstore only.  A project that needs
one folder on the store to carry its own type (the sleep-wallpaper folder the
display HAL reads) therefore cannot get that label.

Set SE_SBGENFS whenever security_fs_use() chose SECURITY_FS_USE_GENFS.  The
default "genfscon vfat /" still labels every other path on such a mount
exactly as before; filesystems using xattr, mount-point or none behaviour are
not touched.  A path with no matching genfscon entry also keeps the
filesystem's default label.

--- a/security/selinux/hooks.c
+++ b/security/selinux/hooks.c
@@ -764,6 +764,18 @@
 
 		sbsec->def_sid = defcontext_sid;
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Filesystems without xattr support (vfat on the user store) carry
+	 * their labels from genfscon, which only applies when the superblock
+	 * is marked SE_SBGENFS.  The 3.0.35 code marks proc/debugfs/sysfs/
+	 * pstore only, so a genfscon path on vfat can never match.  Mark the
+	 * superblock whenever the filesystem's behaviour is GENFS: the default
+	 * "genfscon vfat /" still labels everything else on the mount as
+	 * before, and filesystems with another behaviour are untouched.
+	 */
+	if (sbsec->behavior == SECURITY_FS_USE_GENFS)
+		sbsec->flags |= SE_SBGENFS;
 
 	rc = sb_finish_set_opts(sb);
